      "reference_answer": "Sound localization estimates a sound source's location and, in virtual reality, helps the user perceive the orientation and position of objects by matching auditory and visual cues. When these cues do not match, computer-generated stimuli are less likely to be perceived as real-world stimuli, so presence is broken. This mismatch can also cause cybersickness.",
