      "question": "How do spatial steering-based navigation and physical steering-based navigation differ in how the user controls direction and speed?",
      "reference_answer": "Both types continuously control direction and speed while the user moves. Spatial steering uses body-based signals, such as gaze, hand gestures, or body lean, to determine travel. Physical steering uses separate hardware or setups, such as bike locomotion platforms or VR simulators, where moving the controls changes virtual travel.",
      "concepts": ["steering-based navigation", "spatial steering-based navigation", "physical steering-based navigation"]
